WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.967
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book three.

2
00:00:05.267 --> 00:00:08.874
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.174 --> 00:00:14.253
Unit nine: Time Management. Today you will give advice with imperatives.

4
00:00:14.553 --> 00:00:17.089
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.033 --> 00:00:21.626
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:22.483 --> 00:00:23.821
Prioritize.

7
00:00:24.817 --> 00:00:27.548
Prioritize means to decide what is most important.

8
00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:30.463
Prioritize your homework before games.

9
00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:33.702
Your turn. Say: Prioritize.

10
00:00:36.567 --> 00:00:37.765
Prioritize.

11
00:00:38.517 --> 00:00:39.645
To-do list.

12
00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:43.578
To-do list means a list of tasks you need to do.

13
00:00:44.183 --> 00:00:46.183
I write a to-do list every morning.

14
00:00:46.783 --> 00:00:49.412
Your turn. Say: To-do list.

15
00:00:52.267 --> 00:00:53.349
To-do list.

16
00:00:54.083 --> 00:00:55.003
Deadline.

17
00:00:56.017 --> 00:00:59.084
Deadline means the last time or day to finish something.

18
00:00:59.683 --> 00:01:01.880
The deadline for the project is Friday.

19
00:01:02.483 --> 00:01:05.321
Your turn. Say: Deadline.

20
00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:09.295
Deadline.

21
00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:11.272
Procrastination.

22
00:01:12.283 --> 00:01:15.188
Procrastination means delaying things you should do now.

23
00:01:15.783 --> 00:01:18.143
Procrastination makes me stressed.

24
00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:21.553
Your turn. Say: Procrastination.

25
00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:25.854
Procrastination.

26
00:01:26.617 --> 00:01:27.502
Efficient.

27
00:01:28.517 --> 00:01:31.201
Efficient means working well without wasting time.

28
00:01:31.817 --> 00:01:34.501
Be efficient: do one task at a time.

29
00:01:35.117 --> 00:01:37.618
Your turn. Say: Efficient.

30
00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:41.503
Efficient.

31
00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:43.298
Time-block.

32
00:01:44.283 --> 00:01:47.931
Time-block means to plan fixed times for each task.

33
00:01:48.517 --> 00:01:50.632
I time-block my evening for study.

34
00:01:51.217 --> 00:01:53.706
Your turn. Say: Time-block.

35
00:01:56.567 --> 00:01:57.568
Time-block.

36
00:01:58.317 --> 00:01:59.445
Distraction.

37
00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:03.355
Distraction means something that takes your attention away.

38
00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:06.054
My phone is a big distraction.

39
00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:09.476
Your turn. Say: Distraction.

40
00:02:12.333 --> 00:02:13.567
Distraction.

41
00:02:14.317 --> 00:02:15.712
Multitasking.

42
00:02:16.717 --> 00:02:20.214
Multitasking means doing several things at the same time.

43
00:02:20.817 --> 00:02:23.350
Multitasking often makes mistakes.

44
00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:26.533
Your turn. Say: Multitasking.

45
00:02:29.367 --> 00:02:30.762
Multitasking.

46
00:02:31.517 --> 00:02:32.611
Productivity.

47
00:02:33.617 --> 00:02:36.696
Productivity means how much useful work you do.

48
00:02:37.283 --> 00:02:39.585
Good sleep increases productivity.

49
00:02:40.183 --> 00:02:43.172
Your turn. Say: Productivity.

50
00:02:46.033 --> 00:02:47.127
Productivity.

51
00:02:47.883 --> 00:02:48.838
Goal-setting.

52
00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:52.523
Goal-setting means deciding what you want to achieve.

53
00:02:53.117 --> 00:02:54.884
Goal-setting gives me direction.

54
00:02:55.483 --> 00:02:58.287
Your turn. Say: Goal-setting.

55
00:03:01.133 --> 00:03:02.262
Goal-setting.

56
00:03:03.017 --> 00:03:03.936
Routine.

57
00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:08.494
Routine means the things you do regularly in the same order.

58
00:03:09.083 --> 00:03:11.257
My morning routine starts at six.

59
00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:14.317
Your turn. Say: Routine.

60
00:03:17.167 --> 00:03:18.168
Routine.

61
00:03:18.917 --> 00:03:19.883
Discipline.

62
00:03:20.883 --> 00:03:24.044
Discipline means controlling yourself to do what you should.

63
00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:27.242
Discipline helps me finish on time.

64
00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:30.398
Your turn. Say: Discipline.

65
00:03:33.233 --> 00:03:34.385
Discipline.

66
00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:38.723
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:39.583 --> 00:03:41.490
Visal, how do you manage your time?

68
00:03:42.583 --> 00:03:45.872
Honestly, I struggle with procrastination.

69
00:03:46.983 --> 00:03:51.595
Here's my advice: write a to-do list and prioritize your tasks.

70
00:03:52.683 --> 00:03:54.602
Should I do many things at once?

71
00:03:55.717 --> 00:04:00.519
No. Avoid multitasking. Time-block your evening, and turn off your phone.

72
00:04:01.617 --> 00:04:05.337
Thanks! I'll be more efficient and meet every deadline.

73
00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:08.244
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:09.083 --> 00:04:11.919
Grammar focus: Imperatives for advice.

75
00:04:12.219 --> 00:04:13.348
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:15.852
Prioritize your tasks.

77
00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:18.959
Avoid distractions while studying.

78
00:04:19.850 --> 00:04:22.047
Don't leave everything until the deadline.

79
00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:27.719
Imperatives start with the base verb. For negative advice, use 'Don't' or 'Avoid'.

80
00:04:28.483 --> 00:04:32.366
Be careful! Don't say: Prioritizing your tasks!

81
00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:36.961
Say: Prioritize your tasks!

82
00:04:37.261 --> 00:04:39.075
Imperatives use the base verb.

83
00:04:39.867 --> 00:04:42.554
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:43.367 --> 00:04:44.902
Beat Procrastination.

85
00:04:45.202 --> 00:04:47.376
Time management starts with goal-setting.

86
00:04:48.367 --> 00:04:51.330
Prioritize your to-do list, and check every deadline.

87
00:04:52.333 --> 00:04:55.134
Avoid multitasking and other distractions.

88
00:04:56.133 --> 00:04:58.934
Time-block your day so that you are more efficient.

89
00:04:59.933 --> 00:05:03.129
A clear routine and discipline keep productivity high.

90
00:05:04.233 --> 00:05:08.351
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:09.217 --> 00:05:10.903
blank your tasks first.

92
00:05:11.203 --> 00:05:16.249
A, Prioritize. B, Prioritizing. C, To prioritize.

93
00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:22.148
The answer is A: Prioritize.

94
00:05:23.283 --> 00:05:25.445
Delaying things you should do now is blank.

95
00:05:25.745 --> 00:05:30.374
A, procrastination. B, productivity. C, a routine.

96
00:05:33.933 --> 00:05:36.606
The answer is A: procrastination.

97
00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:40.179
The last day to finish something is the blank.

98
00:05:40.479 --> 00:05:44.411
A, deadline. B, to-do list. C, routine.

99
00:05:47.967 --> 00:05:49.792
The answer is A: deadline.

100
00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:54.140
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:54.983 --> 00:05:57.726
What time management strategy helps you the most?

102
00:06:06.517 --> 00:06:08.017
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:08.317 --> 00:06:17.761
Making a to-do list helps me the most. My advice is simple: write your tasks, do the hardest one first, and avoid your phone.

104
00:06:18.061 --> 00:06:19.747
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:25.067
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and imperatives for advice.

106
00:06:25.367 --> 00:06:30.341
Today's value is time management. Plan your day and use your time well.

107
00:06:30.641 --> 00:06:32.957
See you in Unit ten. Goodbye!

108
00:06:33.257 --> 00:06:36.258
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

